# Installed system fstab. sonora-install renders it with sonora-rootfs.sh
# (render_fstab); the @...@ markers are replaced by UUIDs, never by device
# names, so a different port order on the next boot cannot mount the wrong disk.
# noatime: a read must not become a journal write. commit=60: the journal is
# flushed once a minute, not every five seconds; recording data is flushed by
# the engine's own disk thread, and vm.dirty_* (99-sonora.conf) bounds the rest.
# No "discard": inline TRIM stalls the disk thread; fstrim.timer does it weekly.
UUID=@ROOT_UUID@  /          ext4  noatime,commit=60,errors=remount-ro  0 1
UUID=@ESP_UUID@   /boot/efi  vfat  umask=0077,noatime,nofail             0 2
@SWAP_LINE@
